   "reason": "Second independent blind reviewer (arm B) did not uphold this exact version: [{\"field\": \"later_events[0] / research_rationale / member earlier_end_check (search honesty and earlier-end test)\", \"claim_says\": \"EO 8905 \\\"does not revoke or shorten the earlier order\\\"; \\\"No held instrument revokes this exemption before its term ran\\\"; the OFR catalog search is listed with no hit reported\", \"source_says\": \"The held Office of the Federal Register disposition note for EO 8538 (jobs/later-events/output/EDGES.csv, edge LE-7cd5b97b80e4, verbatim note item) reads \\\"Revoked by: EO 8905, September 22, 1941\\\"; the packet records 2 machine hits for this order in that search. Taken at face value it gives an end on 1941-09-22, earlier than the claimed 1941-09-30. The claim neither discloses nor rebuts this held contrary lead. On the texts the further exemption (one year ending 1942-09-30) appears to be a new grant that does not cut short the old term, so 1941-09-30 may well be the right end, but the claim has to state the OFR note and give reasons for rejecting it.\"}]"
  },
  {
   "instrument_id": "EO:8907",
   "outcome": "blocked",
   "reason": "[\"Transcription differs from the official GPO printing in one figure inside the claim's quoted whole-order span: the APP text (jobs/app-executive-orders/output/texts/executive-order-8907-exemption-william-c-alden-from-compulsory-retirement-for-age.txt, chars 495-498) reads '47 Stat. 382, 401' while the GPO printing (jobs/photius-gpo-volumes/output/texts/EO_8907.txt, line 27, 'section 204 of the act of June 30, 1932, 47 Stat. 382, 404') reads 404 (every sibling exemption order cites 404). Number, title, date (September 24, 1941), signatory, operative text and the end date (September 30, 1942) agree; the difference is a statutory page citation, but the quoted span cannot be confirmed as a faithful transcription. Needs re-basing of the claim on the official printing or an owner decision that the citation typo is immaterial.\"]"
  },
