   "reason": "[\"Transcription is complete and agrees with the official Federal Register printing (46 FR 47207-47208): Sec. 2 is present in the APP text (heading 'Sec. 2. Functions.' is run onto the end of Sec. 1(d) in one line, which is why Lachmann's machine record reads numbering_gap section 1 -> 3); wording, date (September 22, 1981) and signature agree. Remaining gap: the later event EO 12366 (47 FR 23135, amendment of Sec. 1(b) from 11 to 12 members, May 25, 1982), cited on clause CLAUSES:EO:12323#sec1-b, has no source the packet registers with an exact grade and a byte-verifiable custody: the fr-originals 12366 text is ungraded and needs_page_check=true, and shares its PDF hash with the tischendorf declaration (acceptable_as_original false, no text_sha256) so it is rejected as working_text_fragment_identity_or_grade_mismatch; the tischendorf text is rejected for the same missing text_sha256; the APP/clause-draft 12366 text (sha256 b1743ec8...) is grade-exact but the actual claim checker reports source_held:custody_record_only for it (page bytes not held). The EO 12399 later event was re-cited to the official FR text (fr-originals/output/texts/EO_12399.txt, 48 FR 379-380; Sec. 4(h) revokes, Sec. 6 effective Dec. 31, 1982) and passes.\"]"
